{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3054","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3054","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3054\",\"parent_revision\":\"f8e1d27e90ca50308b54549d2a3fda2a73bde1e3\",\"root_revision\":\"b97b5be773066ecc2e71fc6346de923c524d249e13419a910610965c14ce98fe\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe plugin's documentation does not describe its own structure. There is no component map. Eight code packages exist (`agent_profile`, `backlog_core`, `dh_core`, `dispatch_schema`, `hooks`, `progressive_markdown`, `sam_schema`, `scripts`); exactly one of them has an `ARCHITECTURE.md`. Nothing states what each package owns, what it consumes, which packages are near-duplicates of each other, or where the authoritative detail for each lives.\\n\\nThe consequence is measurable and was demonstrated repeatedly in a single session: an agent starting work reads whichever package it lands in, treats that package's behaviour as the system's behaviour, and generalises incorrectly. Specific failures observed, each traceable to a missing line of a component map:\\n\\n- The markdown engine (`progressive_markdown`) was not discovered until late, by accident, after a search in a sibling directory failed. Work was nearly started to build a capability that already existed and was fully tested.\\n- Two distinct markdown handling paths \u2014 storage-key resolution and navigation indexing \u2014 were conflated, producing a confident and wrong claim that the system handled only two heading levels.\\n- A duplicate test file was created because only one of the plugin's six test roots was searched.\\n- A new architecture document was committed with no deduplication against two sibling documents it overlapped, no cross-references, and no entry in any discovery index.\\n- Two committed documents were found to state directly contradictory behaviour, discovered only incidentally.\\n\\nThis item covers the systematic pass. It is deliberately sequenced after the targeted markdown-consumption architecture work so that the smaller, well-understood surface is settled first and can serve as the pattern.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-20T06:07:30.248822Z</sub>\\n\\nCLAIM: Eight code packages exist (agent_profile, backlog_core, dh_core, dispatch_schema, hooks, progressive_markdown, sam_schema, scripts); exactly one of them has an ARCHITECTURE.md\\n\\nVERDICT: VERIFIED\\n\\nEVIDENCE:\\n  - Source: /Users/jamienelson/repos/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness\\n  - Retrieved: 2026-08-20\\n  - Content: All 8 packages verified present. ARCHITECTURE.md present in exactly one (backlog_core).\\n    ```\\n    agent_profile: no ARCHITECTURE.md\\n    backlog_core: HAS ARCHITECTURE.md (63k)\\n    dh_core: no ARCHITECTURE.md\\n    dispatch_schema: no ARCHITECTURE.md\\n    hooks: no ARCHITECTURE.md\\n    progressive_markdown: no ARCHITECTURE.md\\n    sam_schema: no ARCHITECTURE.md\\n    scripts: no ARCHITECTURE.md\\n    ```\\n\\n---\\n\\nCLAIM: A duplicate test file was created because only one of the plugin's six test roots was searched.\\n\\nVERDICT: VERIFIED\\n\\nEVIDENCE:\\n  - Source: git log for plugins/development-harness/tests/test_ordinal_mapper.py\\n  - Retrieved: 2026-08-20\\n  - Content: Test file created in tests/ directory (commit faf346d19 on 2026-08-20 08:15:34), then moved to backlog_core/tests/unit/ (commit 31c14a2df on 2026-08-20 12:11:58 with message \\\"move ordinal property test into existing suite\\\").\\n  - Six test roots confirmed: backlog_core/tests, sam_schema/tests, skills/kage-bunshin/tests, tests (root), tests_backlog, tests_sam\\n\\n---\\n\\nCLAIM: The markdown engine (progressive_markdown) was not discovered until late, by accident, after a search in a sibling directory failed. Work was nearly started to build a capability that already existed and was fully tested.\\n\\nVERDICT: VERIFIED (engine exists and is tested; chronology claim unverified but corroborated by duplicate-test timeline)\\n\\nEVIDENCE:\\n  - Source: /Users/jamienelson/repos/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/progressive_markdown/ and test locations\\n  - Retrieved: 2026-08-20\\n  - Content: progressive_markdown package exists with 13 source modules. Tests exist but distributed across multiple test roots rather than co-located:\\n    - tests_sam/test_progressive_markdown.py\\n    - backlog_core/tests/unit/progressive_markdown/ (multiple test files: test_init_docstring.py, test_indexer_decomposition.py, test_ambiguous_section_ref.py, test_navigation_result_unification.py, and others)\\n  - Tests span 6 test roots, confirming the \\\"only one searched\\\" failure mode.\\n\\n---\\n\\nCLAIM: A new architecture document was committed with no deduplication against two sibling documents it overlapped, no cross-references, and no entry in any discovery index.\\n\\nVERDICT: VERIFIED (overlapping documents confirmed; deduplication status as stated unverified but timeline corroborates)\\n\\nEVIDENCE:\\n  - Source: git log for plugins/development-harness/docs/component-architecture.md and backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md\\n  - Retrieved: 2026-08-20\\n  - Content: component-architecture.md added in commit db2d7fae3 (2026-08-20, \\\"add component architecture map and bind contract scope\\\") without documented cross-reference to backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md (63k, extensive existing documentation). Both files describe component architecture and relationships. Additional file: docs/workflow-architecture-diagram.md (23k) also describes architecture aspects, creating three overlapping architecture documents at different scopes.\\n\\n---\\n\\nCLAIM: Two committed documents were found to state directly contradictory behaviour, discovered only incidentally.\\n\\nVERDICT: INCONCLUSIVE\\n\\nEVIDENCE:\\n  - Source: backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md, docs/component-architecture.md, docs/workflow-architecture-diagram.md\\n  - Retrieved: 2026-08-20\\n  - Content: Three overlapping architecture documents identified in codebase. Claim of direct contradiction not directly verifiable from file presence alone; would require detailed content comparison across both files to confirm specific contradictions. No grep-discoverable markers (e.g., \\\"contradicts\\\", \\\"conflict\\\", \\\"disputed\\\") in commit messages or PR descriptions from this session linking these documents explicitly.\\n  - Cross-check: Research section of this item noted \\\"three existing, already-diverging conventions\\\" pre-existing this session, suggesting divergence is pre-existing rather than newly-discovered, requiring chronological verification of when contradictions surfaced.\\n\\n---\\n\\nCLAIM (from task context): PR #3080's CONTEXT-MAP.md is rooted at the monorepo root, not the plugin root, violating docs/plugin-deployment-model.md.\\n\\nVERDICT: PARTIALLY VERIFIED\\n\\nEVIDENCE:\\n  - Source: CONTEXT-MAP.md at /Users/jamienelson/repos/claude_skills/CONTEXT-MAP.md (repository root, not plugins/development-harness/)\\n  - Retrieved: 2026-08-20\\n  - Content: CONTEXT-MAP.md is a documentation registry/index file pointing to ./plugins/development-harness/CONTEXT.md. No plugin scripts reference or import this file.\\n  - Deployment model constraint: plugin-deployment-model.md \u00a73 prohibits scripts from reaching outside plugin directory tree to paths like \\\"repo root\\\".\\n  - Finding: CONTEXT-MAP.md location does violate the \\\"zip-and-move test\\\" if plugins are expected to reference it. However, no plugin code currently depends on it, making it a documentation-only violation. The file serves as a top-level knowledge index, not a plugin runtime artifact.\\n\\n---\\n\\nCROSS_CHECK:\\n  - Verified test-root count against actual filesystem and git history (6 confirmed)\\n  - Verified package count and ARCHITECTURE.md distribution using `for` loop (1 confirmed)