olved \u2014 not yet merged, but content-complete and stable)\\n2. Whether all 8 code packages currently have at least summary-level architecture coverage | Status: AVAILABLE (verified true for a package-level summary \u2014 component-architecture.md, added this session, covers all 8; per-package depth beyond that summary is what this item's Deliverable 1 still requires)\\n3. Whether a concept glossary exists anywhere in the plugin | Status: AVAILABLE (verified true \u2014 plugins/development-harness/CONTEXT.md, widened this session from markdown-consumption-only to whole-plugin scope; contains the SAM term plus the markdown-consumption vocabulary; the other packages' terms remain to be added, which is this item's Deliverable 2 work, not a blocker)\\n4. Shared root path and naming convention for per-module architecture docs across all 8 packages | Status: AVAILABLE \u2014 RESOLVED this session. Decision: one CONTEXT.md per PLUGIN (the distributable unit), not one per internal package. The 8 code packages (agent_profile, backlog_core, dh_core, dispatch_schema, hooks, progressive_markdown, sam_schema, scripts) are one internal toolset sharing the plugin's single vocabulary, not 8 separate bounded contexts. Root CONTEXT-MAP.md indexes across plugins (multi-plugin monorepo), not across packages within one plugin. plugins/development-harness/CONTEXT.md and CONTEXT-MAP.md were both updated this session to reflect this scope. This item's Deliverable 2 work is therefore: extend the existing CONTEXT.md with the remaining 7 packages' vocabulary, not create 8 separate files.\\n5. Documentation-versus-behaviour drift audit status outside the markdown-consumption area | Status: AVAILABLE (verified: not started \u2014 only the markdown-consumption docs were audited this session; this is the item's own Deliverable 4 scope)\\n6. Cross-reference/duplicate-source table for the whole plugin | Status: AVAILABLE (verified: does not exist yet; this item's own Deliverable 5 scope)\\nAVAILABLE count: 6\\nDERIVABLE count: 0\\nMISSING count: 0\\nVerdict: READY \u2014 proceed to Wave 3 (groomer)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Issue Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-20T06:05:39.448548Z</sub>\\n\\n**Type**: missing-guardrail\\n\\n**Rationale**: The five distinct failures documented (late engine discovery, conflated paths, duplicate test file, uncoordinated docs, contradictory docs) are not caused by broken code but by the absence of documentation structure\u2014specifically a component map, naming conventions, and discovery index. The system works but lacks guardrails (structural conventions, cross-references, indexes) that should prevent agent confusion about module boundaries and coordination gaps. This is a design-gap classification, not a defect.\\n\\n**Analysis Method**: N/A \u2014 missing-guardrail type requires no root-cause analysis.\\n\\n**Scenario Target**: Agents starting work on development-harness read one isolated module, treat its behavior as system behavior, and generalize incorrectly, producing confusion about boundaries, duplicate work, and contradictory docs (five instances observed) \u2192 After implementing component map, per-package architecture docs, shared naming convention, discovery index, and cross-reference table, agents navigate the 8-package structure correctly and avoid module confusion and coordination gaps.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact Radius\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-20T06:12:35.072086Z</sub>\\n\\n### Code - Producers\\n\\nProducers here are the documentation artifacts this item authors, rewrites, or restructures \u2014 not application code. Each becomes the authoritative source other files must not restate.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/component-architecture.md` - Deliverable 1's 8-package map already exists (added PR #3056, currently under review) but is incomplete: `dh_core`, `dispatch_schema`, `agent_profile`, `hooks`, `scripts` get one-sentence role statements with no owns/consumes/consumed-by/detail-location breakdown the