ing variant. Referenced\\nby related item #3050 (\\\"ADR identifiers referenced but undefined \u2014 a subset of the same problem\\\").\\n\\n### Codebase Audit \u2014 the generic convention this session drew from\\n\\nRead directly from the installed skill `mattpocock-skills:domain-modeling`'s SKILL.md\\n(`~/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-plugins-official/mattpocock-skills/1.2.3/skills/engineering/domain-modeling/SKILL.md`).\\nIts prescribed file structure:\\n\\n- Single-context repos: root `CONTEXT.md` + root `docs/adr/NNNN-slug.md`.\\n- Multi-context repos: root `CONTEXT-MAP.md` pointing to each context, where **each context is a\\n  `src/{context}/` subdirectory** containing its own `CONTEXT.md` and `docs/adr/`; system-wide\\n  ADRs stay at the repo root's `docs/adr/`.\\n\\nThe skill's own file-structure example equates \\\"a context\\\" with \\\"a directory\\\" 1:1 \u2014 it assumes\\ndomain boundaries align with source-directory boundaries.\\n\\n### The discriminating tension (why this is a real design decision, not a lookup)\\n\\nThis plugin's actual domains do not align 1:1 with its 8 code packages. The one domain modeled so\\nfar (\\\"markdown consumption\\\") spans 3 packages. Applying the generic skill's per-directory-context\\npattern literally would fragment that vocabulary into 3 separate per-package `CONTEXT.md` files\\nwith no single owner for shared terms (e.g. \\\"Provider\\\", used identically across all three) \u2014\\ndirectly violating this item's Deliverable 2 (\\\"one definition per concept, stated once... every\\nother document links to the definition rather than restating it\\\"). This session's actual choice \u2014\\none root `CONTEXT.md` per cross-cutting *domain*, not per package \u2014 already deviates from the\\ngeneric skill's literal example, for exactly this reason, independent of whether that deviation\\nwas made deliberately.\\n\\nBy contrast, Deliverable 1 (per-package role/owns/consumes/consumed-by/detail-location) aligns\\nnaturally with package boundaries \u2014 this is already how `docs/component-architecture.md` (summary)\\n+ per-package `ARCHITECTURE.md` (detail, precedent (a) above) work today for `backlog_core`. A\\nsingle directory-unit convention that forces both deliverables onto the same unit (e.g. always\\n`<package>/CONTEXT.md`) will misfit whichever of the two deliverables does not naturally align with\\nthat unit. Evidence supports treating architecture-detail placement (package-aligned) and glossary\\nplacement (domain-aligned, which may span packages) as two different axes, not one shared rule \u2014\\nthis is the design decision RT-ICA condition 4 flags as MISSING; this note surfaces the evidence,\\nit does not choose between the axes for the human/rtica-assessor.\\n\\n### Quantitative Impact\\n\\nBaseline (measured via `wc -c`/`find`, 2026-08-20, `plugins/development-harness/`):\\n\\n| Artifact | Size (chars) | Est. tokens (\u00f73.5) | Source |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| All `.md` files in plugin (excl. `__pycache__`) | \u2014 | \u2014 | `find . -iname \\\"*.md\\\"` \u2192 244 files |\\n| `skills/*/SKILL.md` (agent-facing prose, in scope per Deliverable 4's \\\"prose instruction\\\") | \u2014 | \u2014 | `find skills -iname SKILL.md` \u2192 59 files |\\n| `docs/*.md` (root docs, non-recursive) | 393,717 | ~112,491 | `find docs -maxdepth 1 -iname \\\"*.md\\\" -exec wc -c` \u2192 25 files |\\n| `docs/adrs/*.md` | \u2014 | \u2014 | 6 files |\\n| `backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md` (per-package detail precedent) | 63,120 | ~18,034 | `wc -c` |\\n| `backlog_core/DOCUMENTATION_DRIFT_AUDIT.md` (per-package drift-audit precedent) | 28,002 | ~8,001 | `wc -c` |\\n| `CONTEXT.md` (1 domain, spans 3 packages) | 3,600 | ~1,029 | `wc -c` |\\n| `docs/component-architecture.md` (all-8-package summary) | 8,189 | ~2,340 | `wc -c` |\\n\\nContext injection cost tier (per this skill's tiering): `docs/component-architecture.md` at\\n~2,340 tokens = Notable. `backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md` at ~18,034 tokens